# Cyrius Field Notes — Language Gotchas (semantics & runtime)
# Var lifetime + scope, struct locals, init order, fn main, static `var buf[N]`
# inside library fns, the allocator's process-lifetime persistence + arena
# exhaustion policy, i64::MIN arithmetic, and thread handle lifetime.
# Refreshed 2026-08-07 at v6.5.10: the global bump allocator has CHAINED
# CHUNKS since v6.1.19 (measured — 400 MB in 100 MB bites succeeds), so the
# old "exhaust the heap segment in 9 allocs" story no longer describes it;
# three entries added from v6.5.8/.9.
# 33 entries (DERIVED at 6.6.16: grep -c "^\[\[entries\]\]"; this line read 27 while the file held
# 30, and earlier 17 while it held 18).
# v6.6.16: +3 entries — closure_returns_belong_to_the_closure_since_6_6_16, pair_callee_any_spelling_6_6_16,
# typed_pointer_local_slot_v6616 (its `p + n` step table SUPERSEDED at 6.6.17 by sizeof(T) everywhere —
# language/features.cyml typed_pointer_step_is_sizeof_t_v6617). Updated: the `_str` suffix entry (what "Str-typed" means — globals,
# fields, call results; the dispatcher's capture rung), global_init_order_silent_zero (enum-naming
# and all-constant struct / array initializers are baked; the x86 kernel late-replay warning).
# v6.7.7: +3 entries — a_tuple_is_a_value_only_as_a_tuple_v677, stack_pair_store_refused_everywhere_v677,
# a_default_belongs_to_the_definition_v677. Updated: pair_callee_any_spelling_6_6_16 (its "a top-level bind is
# not refused" line, stale since 6.7.6). 36 entries (DERIVED at 6.7.7).
# v6.7.8: +2 entries — a_dyn_holds_an_address_or_a_value_v678 (forming, the dangling `&local`, a scalar's
# value, where a dyn result may go), a_slice_is_a_fn_local_and_reads_signed_elements_signed_v678 (stores
# checked in every build, the sign-extended read, the positions). Updated: typed_pointer_local_slot_v6616
# (`*p` at the element's width, `p[i]`), var_name_bracket_is_bytes_not_elements (a bare array takes no
# subscript; N under the bounds-checked mode), generic_using_t_as_a_struct_has_no_i64_instance (the carrier
# field `b.v.y`, filed). 38 entries (DERIVED at 6.7.8).
# v6.6.5: `private` covers the whole file, and forward references are checked; a struct
# declared inside a fn is per call and per thread, and an over-budget array local warns that
# its storage is static.
# v6.7.10: +1 entry — struct_handles_and_values_since_6_7_10 (the handle line at every size: an integer or an
# untyped carrier of a small struct's word now makes a HANDLE; packed u8..u32 / f32 fields; a field / dereference
# left operand dispatches; an untyped `var c = a + b;` is the struct). Updated:
# struct_field_types_checked_and_f64_fields_typed_since_6_6_10 (its "widths are unchanged" note). 39 entries
# (DERIVED at 6.7.10).
# v6.7.11: +5 entries — multi_value_returns_and_struct_words_since_6_7_11, call_arguments_and_fn_pointer_results_
# since_6_7_11, struct_copies_and_operator_results_since_6_7_11, generics_and_the_frontend_since_6_7_11,
# a_write_length_is_bytes_not_characters_v6711. Updated: var_name_bracket_is_bytes_not_elements (cyrlint's overrun
# rule), vector_value_return_binding_forms (a vector local takes a vector), float_builtin_results_are_float_operands_
# since_6_6_10 (the argument warning), fn_main_is_not_the_entry_point (cx), generic_using_t_as_a_struct_has_no_i64_
# instance (carrier fields, methods). 44 entries (DERIVED at 6.7.11).
# v6.7.12: +2 entries — a_same_value_redeclaration_is_silent_by_design_v6712 (D30), a_stack_enum_cannot_be_its_own_fns_
# return_annotation_v6712 (D23). Updated: call_arguments_and_fn_pointer_results_since_6_7_11 (a vector value into `*V`
# is an address, D27; D28), generics_and_the_frontend_since_6_7_11 (`var q = p;` is a typed copy, D29),
# vector_value_return_binding_forms (Windows' unreceived vector call), var_name_bracket_is_bytes_not_elements (cyrlint's
# N and top-level arrays), an_over_budget_array_local_is_static_storage_and_says_so (two buffers in one fn),
# println_dispatches_on_the_declared_return_type (`println(vec_get(..))`). 46 entries (DERIVED at 6.7.12).
# v6.7.13: +3 entries — struct_values_and_receives_since_6_7_13 (the structs and receives + closures lanes),
# multi_value_returns_since_6_7_13 (ret2 is the literal, the fall-off, one declared type, a tuple parameter),
# vector_pointers_step_vectors_and_windows_value_form_v6713. Updated: struct_handles_and_values_since_6_7_10 (`&s.f`
# refused), call_arguments_and_fn_pointer_results_since_6_7_11 (`(&mk)` is the known callee; the vector argument
# rules), struct_copies_and_operator_results_since_6_7_11 (the scalar-field scanner fixed; the fix-it),
# generics_and_the_frontend_since_6_7_11 (`var q = G;`; `mkg<i64>(..)` for a vector), vector_value_return_binding_forms
# (method / explicit instance / `*p` bind), multi_value_returns_and_struct_words_since_6_7_11 (the wrapped pair call,
# the inherited default, D13), typed_pointer_local_slot_v6616 (`**pp` off the word list). 49 entries (DERIVED at 6.7.13).
# v6.7.14: +6 entries — generics_since_6_7_14 (type arguments, signatures, `p.m<T>(x)`, what a pointer binds, D1 – D8),
# struct_values_and_inline_str_since_6_7_14 (D17 – D23), receives_and_multi_value_since_6_7_14 (D24 – D30, D42 – D46,
# D53), vector_values_since_6_7_14 (D31 – D41), a_u128_is_not_a_parameter_return_or_field_type_yet_v6714 (D10),
# last_definition_wins_reaches_the_stdlibs_own_callers_v6714 (LIB-3, LIB-4, PL-6). Updated: var_name_bracket_is_bytes_
# not_elements (the overrun the register allocator hides), global_init_order_silent_zero (a constant initializer runs
# nothing at startup, D11), vector_value_return_binding_forms, generic_using_t_as_a_struct_has_no_i64_instance (GN-12,
# GN-14, GN-15, GN-17), a_tuple_is_a_value_only_as_a_tuple_v677 and stack_pair_store_refused_everywhere_v677 (the
# transparent wrap, D45 / D46), multi_value_returns_and_struct_words_since_6_7_11 (the struct-literal message, D12),
# call_arguments_and_fn_pointer_results_since_6_7_11 (`&f` typed as `f(..)`, the value-form sources),
# struct_copies_and_operator_results_since_6_7_11, generics_and_the_frontend_since_6_7_11,
# a_same_value_redeclaration_is_silent_by_design_v6712 (folded values, bool, D9), and the three 6.7.13 entries' "filed,
# 6.7.14" lines. 55 entries (DERIVED at 6.7.14).
# v6.7.15 (2026-10-19, Break 2 repair 5): +5 entries —
# a_zone_redeclaration_is_its_last_constant_from_program_start_v6715 (D2, FE-13, FE-15, FE-16), generics_since_6_7_15
# (GN-1's `>>`, D3 – D13), struct_values_and_inline_str_since_6_7_15 (ST-1's forward calls, `*pp`, D14 – D20, D58, D60),
# receives_since_6_7_15 (D30 – D36, D59, D62), vector_values_since_6_7_15 (D21 – D24, D26 – D29, VC-1). Updated — each
# "filed, 6.7.15" line closed or re-pointed: global_init_order_silent_zero (D2, FE-15, FE-16),
# vector_value_return_binding_forms, a_same_value_redeclaration_is_silent_by_design_v6712 (a named constant compared,
# FE-14; FE-12), struct_values_and_receives_since_6_7_13, multi_value_returns_since_6_7_13 (RC-3),
# generic_using_t_as_a_struct_has_no_i64_instance (GN-17, GN-20), the four 6.7.14 lane entries (generics, structs,
# receives, vectors), a_u128_is_not_a_parameter_return_or_field_type_yet_v6714 (D3, VC-1, FE-4). 60 entries (DERIVED at
# 6.7.15).
# v6.7.16 (2026-10-21, Break 2 repair 6): +4 entries — generics_since_6_7_16 (generic signatures and binding: D1 – D10,
# D85 (a), D88, D92, D93, D97, D102), struct_values_and_inline_str_since_6_7_16 (structs, `Str`, `*(&x)`, narrow values,
# top-level copies, closures: D17 – D21, D68, D70 – D74, D87, D96, D103), receives_since_6_7_16 (tuple parameters,
# `return` errors, struct results through a pointer, chain multi-value, multi-value elements, zone globals: D16, D23,
